# Kiro: folders open in Thunar, web pages and links in Firefox.
# Without a default, Disk Usage Analyzer (baobab, on the Kiro and KIROTUX ISOs) won: it comes first
# alphabetically among the apps that declare inode/directory. This is the lowest-priority mimeapps.list,
# so a desktop's own list (Plasma's kde-mimeapps.list -> Dolphin) and the user's choices still win.
# Web pages had no default either, so DankMaterialShell's dms-open won on alphabet, and outside a DMS
# session it only says "DMS is not running": no page or link opened (Kiro News on picard, 2026-11-19).
[Default Applications]
inode/directory=thunar.desktop
text/html=firefox.desktop
application/xhtml+xml=firefox.desktop
x-scheme-handler/http=firefox.desktop
x-scheme-handler/https=firefox.desktop
